---
source: crates/hibi-cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&repo, &[command, \"--help\"])"
---
$ hibi schema --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
Without a name: list the schema names. With a name: print that JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) and nothing else, in both output formats.

Names: the stored records (claim, mark, retirement, anchor, selector), the configuration files (config, user-config), the standard-input documents (claim-input, mark-input), the error output (error), the provider protocol (unit, provider-request, provider-response, conformance-case), and <command>-output for each command with JSON output.

Usage: hibi schema [OPTIONS] [name]

Arguments:
  [name]
          The schema to print [default: list the names]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Results are the same with and without the cache
---- standard error ----
(empty)
